From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] step5: bf16 x bf16 -> fp32 Triton router GEMM
 (VLLM_HCU_STEP5_BF16_ROUTER, default on)

The router weight is bf16 in the checkpoint and the gate input is bf16, so the
fp32 router GEMM (x.float() @ W.float()) can run on the bf16 matrix cores with
fp32 accumulation and give the same products. Decode-sized M uses split-K with
an in-kernel ordered reduction by the last CTA per tile, so the result stays
deterministic and no memset/reduce kernel is needed.

Decode drops the upcast copy, the rocBLAS fp32 split-K GEMM and its PostGSU
(~31us -> ~10us per layer). Also allow num_warps=1 in the router bias top-k
autotune (16us -> ~9us at decode M).

bs32 64k/4k: prefill 10730 -> 11236 tok/s, ITL 82.23 -> 81.73 ms,
decode 1094.6 -> 1093.6 tok/s (noise); arith eval 31/33/36 of 40.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
